`tempSvg.remove()` is called on the happy path only. If `configureLabelImages` throws (or any other `await` in the function rejects), the hidden `<svg>` element appended to `document.body` at line 68 is never removed, leaking a DOM node on every failure. Wrap the measurement block in a `try/finally` so the cleanup is guaranteed:
```js
try {
  await configureLabelImages(div.node(), node.label);
  // ... bbox measurement ...
  fo.attr('width', bbox.width).attr('height', bbox.height);
} finally {
  tempSvg.remove();
}
return fo.node();
```
